How embeddings are used in a Banking RAG project:  (Complete architecture)

Suppose you have 10,000 pages of banking policy documents. You cannot send all the documents to the LLM for every customer question.

|Document ingestion — performed when indexing or updating documents|
PDF / Word / HTML policy documents
|
Extract text and split into chunks
|
Generate document embeddings
|
Store vectors, text and metadata in a vector database

|Retrieval — performed for each user question|
Customer question
|
Generate query embedding
|
Compare against document vectors and retrieve relevant chunks
|
Send relevant context to the LLM
|
Generate an answer grounded in retrieved policy text

Why is this useful?
- Efficiency: you avoid re-embedding every policy document for each question.
- Semantic retrieval: a question can find relevant text even when it uses different wording.
- Scalability: vector indexes help search large collections efficiently.
- Grounding: the LLM can use retrieved policy content instead of relying only on its pretrained knowledge.

